    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56079" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατοπτρ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>in a mirror</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαντασία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Placit.</u>
					3.1.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμφάσεις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				3.2.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ κ.</span>
			<i>reflected images</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				3.5.6
			</span></i>; but, <i>Theory of Reflexion</i>, title of work by <i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Damian.
				<u>Opt.</u>
				14
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατοπτρ-κή</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>in Euc.</u>
				p.40
			</span></i> F.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατοπτρ-κόν</span></b> ,
				τό, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>
			<i>*Deff.</i><i><span class="en">
				135.12
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>
			<i>by reflexion</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βλέπεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Placit.</u>
					2.24.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
